.vscode

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Kristineberg: GENERATED Unity assets (decision, Ivan 2026-08-17)
#
# These are Unity's import of the site build outputs, ~134 MB in total:
#   kristineberg_buildings.asset        57 MB
#   kristineberg_buildings_col0.asset   43 MB
#   KristinebergTerrain.asset           19 MB
#   kristineberg_buildings_col1.asset   14 MB
#   kristineberg_control.bin             6 MB
#
# The SOURCES are committed (LFS): kristineberg_heightmap.r16 and the .smesh
# meshes, ~38 MB. Everything above is derived from them by
#   SMARC -> Build Kristineberg Site
# so committing both would store the same geometry twice, and 134 MB of binary
# in normal git is permanent — every clone pays for it forever. DrydockHiRes
# already uses ~629 MB of GitHub's 1 GB free LFS tier, so LFS-tracking these was
# not a safe alternative either.
#
# THE COST, STATED PLAINLY: a fresh clone must run the builder menu item once
# before KristinebergEmpty.unity is usable. The builder regenerates the terrain,
# the meshes AND KristinebergWorld.prefab together, so the GUID references
# between them are rebuilt consistently in the same pass — which is why the
# .meta files are ignored alongside their assets rather than kept for GUID
# stability. A .meta without its asset is not stability, it is an orphan.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
Runtime/Terrain/Kristineberg/KristinebergTerrain.asset
Runtime/Terrain/Kristineberg/KristinebergTerrain.asset.meta
Runtime/Terrain/Kristineberg/kristineberg_buildings*.asset
Runtime/Terrain/Kristineberg/kristineberg_buildings*.asset.meta
Runtime/Terrain/Kristineberg/kristineberg_dock*.asset
Runtime/Terrain/Kristineberg/kristineberg_dock*.asset.meta
Runtime/Terrain/Kristineberg/kristineberg_control.bin
Runtime/Terrain/Kristineberg/kristineberg_control.bin.meta

# Asko curated terrain (~544 MB) is NOT in git: it would exceed the 1 GB LFS quota.
# Regenerate with the Asko site pipeline or fetch the Oceanverse bundle. (2026-09-13)
Runtime/Terrain/Asko/
Runtime/Terrain/Asko.meta

# Djurö curated terrain (2026-09-15) is NOT in git, for a reason Askö's entry does not have:
# EVERY cell of it is derived from Sjöfartsverket S-57 charts under the FUK licence
# (research/education, no redistribution, inheritable), so committing it would put restricted
# data in a repo with a GitHub remote — the mistake this project already made once with 7.4 MB
# of FUK-derived GeoJSON. The size argument applies too (the r16 alone is 33.6 MB and the LFS
# quota is nearly spent), but rights are the binding constraint here.
# Regenerate with data-cube/scripts/djuro-site/build_heightmap.py + build_splatmap.py, or fetch
# the Oceanverse bundle smds-cloud-store/scenario-bundles/ov-site-Djuro-curated-v1.
Runtime/Terrain/Djuro/
Runtime/Terrain/Djuro.meta
